.TH "NETPLAN\-APPLY" "8" "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
\f[CR]netplan\-apply\f[R] \- apply configuration from Netplan YAML files
to a running system
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-debug\f[R]] \f[B]apply\f[R]
\f[B]\-h\f[R]|\f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-debug\f[R]] \f[B]apply\f[R]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan apply\f[B]\f[R] applies the current Netplan
configuration to a running system.
.PP
The process works as follows:
.IP "1." 3
The back\-end configuration is generated from Netplan YAML files.
.IP "2." 3
The appropriate back ends (\f[B]\f[CB]systemd\-networkd\f[B]\f[R](8) or
\f[B]\f[CB]NetworkManager\f[B]\f[R](8)) are invoked to bring up
configured interfaces.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan apply\f[B]\f[R] iterates through interfaces that are
still down, unbinding them from their drivers and rebinding them.
This gives \f[B]\f[CB]udev\f[B]\f[R](7) renaming rules the opportunity
to run.
.IP "4." 3
If any devices have been rebound, the appropriate back ends are
re\-invoked in case more matches can be done.
.PP
For information about the generation step, see
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\-generate\f[B]\f[R](8).
For details of the configuration file format, see
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R](5).
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Print basic help.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-debug\f[R]
Print debugging output during the process.
.SH KNOWN ISSUES
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan apply\f[B]\f[R] will not remove virtual devices such
as bridges and bonds that have been created, even if they are no longer
described in the Netplan configuration.
That is due to the fact that Netplan operates statelessly and is not
aware of the previously defined virtual devices.
.PP
This can be resolved by manually removing the virtual device (for
example \f[CR]ip link delete dev bond0\f[R]) and then running
\f[CR]netplan apply\f[R], by rebooting, or by creating a temporary
backup of the YAML state in \f[CR]/etc/netplan\f[R] before modifying the
configuration and passing this state to Netplan (e.g.
\f[CR]mkdir \-p /tmp/netplan_state_backup/etc && cp \-r /etc/netplan /tmp/netplan_state_backup/etc/\f[R]
then running
\f[CR]netplan apply \-\-state /tmp/netplan_state_backup\f[R]).
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R](5),
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\-generate\f[B]\f[R](8),
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\-try\f[B]\f[R](8), \f[B]\f[CB]udev\f[B]\f[R](7),
\f[B]\f[CB]systemd\-networkd.service\f[B]\f[R](8),
\f[B]\f[CB]NetworkManager\f[B]\f[R](8)
